<title>BELGIUM: EU reviews Generali buy of Prime from Fiat.</title>
<headline>EU reviews Generali buy of Prime from Fiat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it was starting a preliminary review of the proposed takeover of Italian investment and life insurance firm Prime SpA by rival insurer Assicurazioni Generali SpA.</p>
<p>It said the deal was submitted for clearance on November 21 under the merger regulation, 4064/89, which bans creation or strengthening of dominant positions. The Commission has one month from that date to clear the operation or start a full, four-month probe.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal announced in October, Generali will acquire Fiat's 95.1 percent stake in Prime, one of Italy's biggest fund managers.</p>
</text>
